From: Michael Froman <mfroman@mozilla.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:40:00 +0000
Subject: Bug 1996020 - use I420Buffer::CreateOrNull in
 VideoFrameBufferPool::CreateI420Buffer. r=bwc

Looking at the crash reports, even after converting DesktopCaptureImpl::OnCaptureResult
to use the VideoFrameBufferPool, we're still seeing occasional crashes
in AlignedMalloc so use CreateOrNull so we don't crash in OOM situations.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326269
Mercurial Revision: https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/93cb056a0c8220b5b364f9cd1204ac34bb0d163d
---
 common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool.cc | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool.cc b/common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool.cc
index 7f65f87302..df349a2d5f 100644
--- a/common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool.cc
+++ b/common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool.cc
@@ -139,8 +139,10 @@ scoped_refptr<I420Buffer> VideoFrameBufferPool::CreateI420Buffer(int width,
   if (buffers_.size() >= max_number_of_buffers_)
     return nullptr;
   // Allocate new buffer.
-  scoped_refptr<I420Buffer> buffer =
-      make_ref_counted<I420Buffer>(width, height);
+  scoped_refptr<I420Buffer> buffer = I420Buffer::CreateOrNull(width, height);
+  if (!buffer) {
+    return nullptr;
+  }
 
   if (zero_initialize_)
     buffer->InitializeData();
